## Biographies
Di Zhao received her B.S. degree in 2011 from Chongqing Normal University, China. Now she is a Master candidate of analytical chemistry at Sichuan University. Her research interests are focused on synthesis of semiconductor nanomaterials and their application in chemical sensor.
Xiangyu Wan received her B.S. degree in 2012 from Sichuan University, China. Now she is a Master candidate of analytical chemistry at Sichuan University. Her current research topic is synthesis of metal–organic frameworks and their applications in gas sensor
Hongjie Song received her Ph.D. from Sichuan University in 2012. Now she works at college of Chemistry, Sichuan University, China. Her current research topic is the use  of composite nanostructures for chemical sensor applications.
Liying Hao received her Master degree in 2013 from Sichuan University, China. Now she works at State Key Laboratory of Oral Diseases, Sichuan University, China. Her research interests are the controllable synthesis of graphene based composite materials and their applications.
Yingying Su received her Ph.D. from Sichuan University in 2007. Now she works at Analytical & Testing Center, Sichuan University, China. Her areas of interest are separation technique, chemiluminescence and luminescence-based sensor.
Yi Lv received his bachelor’s degree, master’s degree and Ph.D. degree from Southwest China Normal University (the current name is Southwest University) in 1997, 2000 and 2003, respectively. After a two-year stay in Tsinghua University as a postdoctoral fellow, he joined the faculty of the College of Chemistry at Sichuan University in 2005. His research interests are mainly in the areas of nanomaterials for analytical chemistry and luminescence-based sensors.
